@startuml
!pragma layout smetana
' Diagram 1: Phase 1 core system overview — layered modular monolith
left to right direction
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam linetype ortho
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam wrapWidth 150
skinparam maxMessageSize 110

actor Customer
actor Agent
actor "Support employee" as Support
actor Admin

component "REST API\nPresentation layer\n20+ endpoints; OpenAPI" as API

package "Business layer — PayLink modular monolith" as PayLink {
  component "Accounts and Wallet\nmanual support block / unblock" as AccountsWallet
  component "Biller Catalog\nbillers, services, service ranges" as BillerCatalog
  component "Payment Processing" as PaymentProcessing
  component "Biller Integration" as BillerIntegration
  component "Fees and Commissions" as FeesCommissions
  component "Notifications" as Notifications
  component "Fraud Checks (extra)\nglobal 5–10,000 EGP range check" as FraudChecks
  component "Reconciliation (extra)" as Reconciliation
}

package "Cross-cutting components (not modules)" as CrossCutting {
  component "Authentication and roles" as AuthRoles
  component "Audit log\nmoney movements: who, when, why" as AuditLog
  component "Configuration store\nfees and limits" as ConfigStore
}

database "Relational database\n(at least 10 tables)" as Database

Customer --> API : REST
Agent --> API : REST
Support --> API : REST
Admin --> API : REST

API --> AuthRoles : authenticate / authorize
API --> AccountsWallet : account / wallet / top-up
API --> BillerCatalog : billers / services
API --> PaymentProcessing : inquiry / pay
API --> BillerIntegration : callback
API --> Reconciliation : support report
API --> ConfigStore : admin configuration

PayLink --> Database
AccountsWallet --> AuditLog : money movements
@enduml

@startuml
!pragma layout smetana
' Diagram 2: Payment Processing and Biller Integration contract — Phase 1
left to right direction
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam packagePadding 30
skinparam linetype ortho
skinparam shadowing false

package "PayLink payment modules" {
  component "Payment Processing\nowns Biller interface\napplies state transitions" as PaymentProcessing
  interface "Biller interface" as BillerPort
  component "Biller Integration\none adapter per biller\nreturns normalized results" as BillerIntegration
  component "Fees and Commissions" as FeesCommissions
}
component "Configuration store\nfee rules" as ConfigStore

PaymentProcessing --> FeesCommissions : fee calculation
ConfigStore --> FeesCommissions : configured fees

PaymentProcessing --> BillerPort : inquiry / pay / query
BillerIntegration ..|> BillerPort : implements with adapters
BillerIntegration --> PaymentProcessing : normalized result
@enduml

@startuml
!pragma layout smetana
' Diagram 3: Per-biller adapters and external file/callback flows — Phase 1
left to right direction
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam linetype ortho
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam wrapWidth 150
skinparam maxMessageSize 115

package "Biller Integration" as Integration {
  component "ElectroCo adapter" as ElectroAdapter
  component "AquaCo adapter" as AquaAdapter
  component "TopUpNet adapter" as TopUpAdapter
  component "NetCo adapter (optional)" as NetCoAdapter
}

package "External billers" {
  component "ElectroCo\nREST / JSON" as ElectroCo
  component "AquaCo\nSOAP-style XML" as AquaCo
  component "TopUpNet\nREST / JSON" as TopUpNet
  component "NetCo (optional)\ndaily batch CSV" as NetCo
}

component "REST API\nTopUpNet callback endpoint" as API
artifact "NetCo result CSV\n(next morning)" as NetCoResult

ElectroAdapter --> ElectroCo : REST / JSON
AquaAdapter --> AquaCo : SOAP-style XML
TopUpAdapter --> TopUpNet : payment request + callback URL
TopUpNet --> API : asynchronous callback
API --> TopUpAdapter : callback payload

NetCoAdapter --> NetCo : daily payment CSV
NetCo --> NetCoResult : sends result
NetCoResult --> NetCoAdapter : processed by adapter

note bottom of Integration
  Adapters hide biller protocols and return normalized results
  through the Biller interface to Payment Processing.
end note
@enduml

@startuml
!pragma layout smetana
' Diagram 4: Fraud check inputs and block ownership — Phase 1
left to right direction
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam linetype ortho
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam wrapWidth 155
skinparam maxMessageSize 120

component "Accounts and Wallet\nstores blocked status; manual support block / unblock" as AccountsWallet
component "Payment Processing\ncomputes daily total" as PaymentProcessing
component "Fraud Checks (extra)\nglobal 5–10,000 EGP range check" as FraudChecks
component "Configuration store\nlimits and fee rules" as ConfigStore

AccountsWallet --> PaymentProcessing : verification / blocked status
PaymentProcessing --> FraudChecks : payment + account context + daily total
FraudChecks --> PaymentProcessing : check result / velocity-block decision
PaymentProcessing --> AccountsWallet : persist automatic velocity block
ConfigStore --> FraudChecks : configured limits

note bottom of FraudChecks
  Fraud Checks decides automatic velocity blocks.
  Accounts and Wallet owns the stored blocked status and manual
  support block / unblock. Payment Processing passes account data
  and the daily total; Fraud Checks does not call Accounts and Wallet.
end note
@enduml

@startuml
!pragma layout smetana
' Diagram 5: Non-blocking notification flow — Phase 1
left to right direction
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam linetype ortho
skinparam shadowing false

component "Payment Processing" as PaymentProcessing
component "Notifications" as Notifications

package "External notification providers" as Providers {
  component "SMS provider" as SMS
  component "Email provider" as Email
  component "Push provider" as Push
}

PaymentProcessing ..> Notifications : non-blocking outcome notice
Notifications --> Providers : deliver message

note bottom of Notifications
  Notification failure never stops or rolls back a payment.
  An SMS or email delivery failure is retried 3 times, then marked undelivered.
end note
@enduml

@startuml
!pragma layout smetana
' Diagram 6: Settlement reconciliation flow — Phase 1
left to right direction
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam linetype ortho
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam wrapWidth 155
skinparam maxMessageSize 125

component "Biller\n(ElectroCo example)" as Biller
artifact "Settlement file" as SettlementFile
component "Reconciliation (extra)" as Reconciliation
component "Payment Processing" as PaymentProcessing
database "Relational database\nPayLink payment records" as Database

Biller --> SettlementFile : sends file
SettlementFile --> Reconciliation : nightly input
Reconciliation --> Database : compare records
Reconciliation --> PaymentProcessing : reconciliation result

note bottom of Reconciliation
  Reconciliation compares the biller file with PayLink records
  and reports differences. Payment Processing applies any
  resulting payment-state transition.
end note

note bottom of SettlementFile
  NetCo's next-morning result CSV is handled by Biller Integration,
  not as this settlement file. See the Biller Integration diagram in this file.
end note
@enduml
